  "text_md": "![](<0f802dfe01644934363d1db3cf8bc60e45e506da_page_13_processed_images/imageFile1.png>)\n\n# Cross border co-ordination\n\n- • Optimum timing of withdrawal likely to vary\n- • Gains from information exchange and coordination:\n\n- – Minimise cross-border distortions and arbitrage\n- – Minimise collective action problems\n- – Largest gains where spillover risks highest (such as deposit insurance and liability guarantees – eg Hong Kong/Singapore/Malaysia co-ordinating removal of exceptional retail deposit insurance)\n\n\n- • Strengthening infrastructure and framework for foreign currency liquidity (G20 group)\n\n\n",
